Lab 1B – Access Control and Encapsulation

1. Private

Private members can only be accessed within their enclosing declaration and its extensions in the same file.

Example: The balance variable in BankAccount is private. This prevents direct modification of the account balance.

2. Fileprivate

Fileprivate members can be accessed anywhere within the same Swift source file.

Example: The fileMessage property in AccessDemo demonstrates fileprivate access.

3. Internal

Internal members can be accessed anywhere within the same module. This is the default access level in Swift.

Example: The internalMessage property can be accessed from main.swift because both files belong to the same module.

4. Public

Public members can be accessed from other modules when the containing type is accessible.

Example: BankAccount is public, and its deposit(), withdraw(), and checkBalance() methods are public.

Conclusion

Access control protects important data and prevents unwanted changes. Encapsulation allows users to interact with an object through controlled methods instead of directly modifying its internal properties.
